<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    What the app claims for Release builds - the ones that reach TestFlight,
    the App Store, and Sideloadly.

    `production` matches what the `cubechat App Store` profile grants, checked
    rather than assumed: the profile's entitlements carry
    `aps-environment: production` and `get-task-allow: false`. A mismatch here
    is not a warning, it is a rejected upload.

    One consequence worth writing down. Sideloading re-signs this binary with a
    free personal profile, which cannot grant `production` - or any
    aps-environment, since push is a paid-account capability. Sideloadly strips
    entitlements its profile cannot cover, so the install still works and push
    stays dead there, which it already was. If an install ever fails right
    after this file appears, that stripping is the first thing to check.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>production</string>
</dict>
</plist>
